<!--
  Every URL on this site that is meant to be found.

  Everything here is readable without an account. The app itself is one
  authenticated shell behind a login and is not listed: a sitemap pointing at
  app routes would be pointing at pages that serve a sign-in form to everybody
  who followed the link.

  No <lastmod>. It would have to say "today" on every deploy, because a build
  rewrites every file's timestamp whether or not a word changed, and a lastmod
  that cries wolf is worse than none — crawlers learn to ignore the field and
  then ignore it on the day it was true. <changefreq> and <priority> are left
  out for the same reason: Google has said publicly it does not use them.
-->
